  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...Dry weather with above normal temperatures \nthrough the weekend under high pressure.\n\nKEY MESSAGE 1 DESCRIPTION...\nThe ridge of high pressure will keep winds light, skies mostly clear \nand temperatures above normal through the weekend. Highs will be in \nthe lower 80s tomorrow for inland locations, and cooler along the \ncoast with a sea breeze developing by afternoon afternoon. Fog has \nslowly dissipated over the waters this afternoon but expect it to \ndevelop again tonight. How far north it is able to drift remains in \nquestion with very little flow through 500mb. This likely to set the \nstage for development right along the coast around midnight.\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2...Potential for a system moving in mid-week,\nbringing another round of wetting rainfall.\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2 DESCRIPTION...\nHigh pressure lingers over the region this weekend, as low \npressure system slides along the east coast early next week. \nGenerally, low pressure east of the Carolinas moves northeast in\nthe Atlantic, east of Nova Scotia. To the north, another low \npressure over Canada moves eastward, as a low over Michigan \nslides east and brings a cold front along its boundary. Wetting \nrainfall expected, with higher totals along Downeast, Tuesday \nnight into Thursday. Potential for 0.5 to 1 inch of rainfall. \nSome isolated thunderstorms are also possible with this system \nWednesday afternoon.",
